SETTINGS screen renders bit-identical (minus a 1px trailing period): fix the panel-overwrite,
palette fade, status-string garbage, and widget-state store-width bugs.

With patches 132/133 the SETTINGS panel was flat-green with only widget boxes.  Root causes (all
asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin / fist_mga_image.bin), each an independent bug:

- 6d65 (status-text element paint, asm 0x6d65): the label-background rect-fill `mov al,0; lcall [0x60a]`
  (MGAVIDEO 0x1091) takes bx = elem+4 (the element's [y0,x0,y1,x1] rect); patch 132 dropped bx and passed
  0, so 1091 filled the rect at DGROUP:0 = a garbage full-screen rect (index 0x19/0xa0) that WIPED the
  SETTINGS.MRL panel every frame.  Thread bx = elem+4.  This is THE panel-overwrite fix.

- 0874 (MGAVIDEO palette fade-in, asm 0x874): the crossfade-target alloc `mov bx,0x788; mov ax,0x300;
  lcall [0xe4]` uses the uninstalled device-alloc vector DGROUP:0xe4 (== 0, a no-op) -> seg788=0 -> 0874
  fell to the present-only path and uploaded the RAW loaded palette.  The original fade settles at
  present=ramp[target] with acc=0xffff == target-1 (a uniform 1-level dim), so the raw upload was +1
  too bright everywhere.  Resolve 0xe4 directly to the real MEMMGR alloc FUN_1000_182a (same pattern as
  the 0x782 alloc at 0009, patch 049), run the fade, and set the c5e8 fade-step far-vector fully so the
  shim retrace ISR (fist_vga.c) can invoke MGAVIDEO 0x0946 each frame until it settles.

- 700a (status-string setter, asm 0x700a `mov [0x8b53],es`): ES is the status-string RESOURCE segment
  returned by the caller's uninstalled far resolve method ([0x2ac]/[0x2e0]/[0x2f0]) -> garbage -> 6d65
  drew a wild string (bottom-row noise).  Thread es = the UI str-seg word[DGROUP:0x70] (=0x2d74).

- 6ef5 (config->widget-state init, asm 0x6ef5): the boolean checkbox flags 0x8b45/46/50/4d/4e/4f are
  BYTE stores (`mov al`) but were typed WORD -> the 0x8b4e word-write clobbered byte[0x8b4f] the previous
  store set, so the SMOKE-EFFECTS (and SKY) checkboxes rendered empty.  Restore the asm byte/word widths.

- 6c38 (joystick status, asm 0x6c38): `mov si,0x165c; lcall [0x2ac]; call 700a` -- [0x2ac] is the status
  resolver, whose reloc section (leading seg 0xf69, table @0x33720) is not installed here, so DGROUP:0x2ac
  == 0 (no-op) and si stayed 0x165c ("SETTINGS NOT CHANGED").  The real target DGROUP:0x2ac = 0xf69:0x444f
  = FUN_1000_444f is an UNDECOMPILED display-list status-message BUILDER (stride-10 node table at
  str-seg:0x360, linked-list ops via 0xf69:0x482f, appends a trailing '.').  Full reconstruction (seed the
  0x2ac/0x2e0/0x2f0 family in SeedServiceVecs + re-decompile + install the reloc section) is a deferred
  frontier; as a PARTIAL reconstruction, resolve the joystick-status TEXT from the game's parallel status
  table at DGROUP:0x8b33 (= [0x1672 "NO JOYSTICK SELECTED", 0x1687 "STANDARD JOYSTICK SELECTED", ...]):
  si = word[0x8b33 + jstype*2].  This yields the correct status text but OMITS 444f's trailing '.', a
  single deterministic 1px delta on the status line -> SETTINGS AE = 1 (not 0).  NOT added to verify.sh.

Result: SETTINGS AE = 1/64000 vs ref/settings_native320.png (deterministic, panel+palette+labels+widgets
+status text all bit-identical; sole delta = the status-line trailing period).

